BT /F1 16 Tf 50 740 Td (Chapter 1: Introduction to Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Tj ET
50 725 m 550 725 l S
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 700 Td (1.1 Executive Overview) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 684 Td (Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) is a state-of-the-art AI architectural pattern that) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 668 Td (combines the parametric memory of Large Language Models \(LLMs\) with non-parametric) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 652 Td (vector databases. By dynamically retrieving external knowledge relevant to a user's prompt,) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 636 Td (RAG mitigates hallucinations and enables real-time access to private enterprise documents.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 608 Td (1.2 Motivation and Business Value) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 592 Td (Standard LLMs suffer from knowledge cutoff dates and frequently hallucinate domain-specific) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 576 Td (facts. RAG solves this by providing grounding context alongside user queries, ensuring) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 560 Td (that answers are factual, auditable, and backed by verifiable citations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 532 Td (1.3 Key Architectural Pillars) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 516 Td (A robust RAG system consists of three primary modules: the Document Ingestion Pipeline,) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 500 Td (the Semantic Vector Store, and the Grounded Synthesis Engine.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 270 30 Td (Page 1 of 5 - RAG Architecture Guide) Tj ET
endstream
