BT /F1 16 Tf 50 740 Td (Chapter 3: Vector Databases and Indexing Mechanisms) Tj ET
50 725 m 550 725 l S
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 700 Td (3.1 Role of Vector Databases) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 684 Td (Vector databases provide specialized storage and approximate nearest neighbor \(ANN\) search.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 668 Td (Popular options include ChromaDB, FAISS, and Qdrant. ChromaDB provides embedded persistence) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 652 Td (with native metadata filtering.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 624 Td (3.2 Hierarchical Navigable Small World \(HNSW\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 608 Td (HNSW graph indexing allows sub-linear search latency across millions of high-dimensional) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 592 Td (vectors by organizing nodes into multi-layer proximity graphs.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 564 Td (3.3 Cosine Similarity vs Euclidean Distance) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 548 Td (Normalized embeddings utilize cosine similarity, computed as the dot product between the) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 532 Td (query vector and chunk vector. A score of 1.0 indicates identical directional semantics,) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 50 516 Td (while scores above 0.70 indicate strong topical alignment.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 270 30 Td (Page 1 of 5 - RAG Architecture Guide) Tj ET
endstream
